A professional ensemble for gold trading should use HMM Pro to identify regime, Wavelet Pro to separate trend/cycle/noise, LSTM to model medium-term sequential behavior, and TFT to produce multi-horizon probabilistic forecasts, with a meta-layer that changes model weights by regime rather than averaging everything equally. Research on TFT and ensemble forecasting supports combining diverse models and using performance-aware weighting, while the TFT framework itself is designed for mixed inputs and multi-horizon forecasting.

Phase 1: System objective
Define the ensemble’s job clearly: it is not four models voting on direction, but a regime-aware alpha engine for XAU/USD that changes emphasis depending on whether the market is in Growth, Normal, or Crisis conditions. A dynamic ensemble is preferable because financial models often work differently across market states, and performance-based weighting is commonly used to emphasize the right model under the right conditions.

