Phase 2: Role definition
Each model must have a different professional responsibility, otherwise the ensemble becomes redundant.

| Model       | Primary role in gold system                                                |
| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Wavelet Pro | Denoise price, extract trend/cycle/noise, quantify structural clarity      |
| HMM Pro     | Identify latent market state and transition probability                    |
| LSTM        | Learn medium-horizon sequential behavior and persistence/reversal patterns |
| TFT         | Produce multi-horizon quantile forecasts and confidence bands              |

This structure is strong because HMM is regime-centric, Wavelet is decomposition-centric, LSTM is memory-centric, and TFT is forecast-plus-uncertainty-centric, so the ensemble is diverse rather than repetitive.

Phase 3: Regime framework
Before assigning weights, define the three operating regimes in a measurable way.

Growth regime
Gold behaves in a more orderly, opportunity-rich environment, often with cleaner trends, lower panic distortion, and more stable macro transmission. This regime should favor models that exploit smooth structure and medium-horizon continuation.

Normal regime
Gold is balanced, mixed, and often alternates between range behavior and moderate trend behavior. This regime should give relatively balanced weights and rely heavily on ensemble confirmation rather than one dominant model.

Crisis regime
Gold becomes driven by macro shocks, liquidity stress, flight-to-safety flows, and regime breaks. In crisis conditions, regime inference, uncertainty forecasting, and noise separation become more important than ordinary sequence fitting.

